  "type": "docs.detail.section",
  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "title": "defineTheme",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "defineTheme creates a theme from explicit token overrides and optional scale configs. Existing themes may use `color` to expand an accent seed into neutral, surface, text, border, and related values; it is not an accent-only edit. Keep that configuration when preserving existing output. For new complete palettes, generate and review a committed palette module, then import its `palette` export and reference stable stops from semantic tokens. This keeps mapped roles coherent when the accepted palette is regenerated; generation itself does not rewrite the theme. Other scale configs generate typography, radius, and motion values from parameters. Explicit token overrides always take precedence over scale-generated values, token by token. When an existing `color` config is in use, overriding `--color-accent` in `tokens` re-points `--color-accent-muted`, `--color-text-accent`, and `--color-icon-accent`, but `--color-on-accent` stays baked from the `color.accent` seed. Prefer a `[light, dark]` tuple for `color.accent` over overriding `--color-accent` alone. localTokens accepts any valid CSS custom-property name; prefixes do not establish ownership."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "tsx",
        "code": "import {defineTheme} from '@astryxdesign/core/theme';\nimport {palette} from './palette.generated';\n\nconst myTheme = defineTheme({\n  name: 'my-theme',\n  typography: {\n    scale: { base: 14, ratio: 1.2 },\n    body: { family: 'Inter', fallbacks: '-apple-system, sans-serif' },\n  },\n  radius: { base: 4, multiplier: 1 },\n  motion: { fast: 175, medium: 410, ratio: 0.75 },\n  tokens: {\n    '--color-background-surface': [\n      palette.neutral.light[100],\n      palette.neutral.dark[15],\n    ],\n  },\n});",
        "label": "defineTheme with generated palette references and non-color scale configs"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Config",
          "Generates",
          "Parameters"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "color (existing themes)",
            "--color-accent, --color-background-*, --color-text-*, --color-border, etc.",
            "Supported broad scale: accent? (hex or [light, dark] tuple), neutralStyle? (warm|cool|neutral), contrast? (standard|high). Use theme palette generate for new complete palettes."
          ],
          [
            "typography.scale",
            "--text-heading-*-size/weight/leading, --text-body-size/weight/leading",
            "base (px), ratio"
          ],
          [
            "typography.body/heading/code",
            "--font-family-body, --font-family-heading, --font-family-code",
            "family, fallbacks?, url?, weight?"
          ],
          [
            "radius",
            "--radius-inner, --radius-element, --radius-container, --radius-page, --radius-chat",
            "base (px), multiplier (0–2)"
          ],
          [
            "motion",
            "Every --duration-* token, --ease-entrance and --ease-move (tempo also times the touch springs)",
            "tempo? (0.75–1.5), character? (crisp|standard|expressive); and/or a duration scale: fast (ms), medium (ms), ratio, slow?, easing?. The scale wins over tempo for the durations it sets, and explicit tokens win over both. Fixed whatever the knobs say: drags and momentum, rubber band, keyboard, press onset/cancel/flash, hover intent, gesture thresholds, Spinner/Skeleton loops, the 200 ms Reduce Motion cap. See `astryx docs motion`."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "For dark mode tuples in token values, see the Dark mode section of `astryx docs use-a-theme`."
      }
    ],
